# Fixed 2026-09-29 by lane 130's merge `0ba7b084` (defect 130); the case is
# defect 133's lane's, one per shape, so that the hang cannot come back
# unseen. Symptom: on the compilers of `a6eab736` and `7c0cb024` the parser
# never returned from this file, measured with a ten-second timeout, and the
# statement list it was building grew for as long as it ran. Cause, read and
# not re-run: a statement headed by a token the lexer refused, right after a
# block, consumed nothing, and the statement's end took the block's own
# dedent, the token before it, for a statement that had ended with a block,
# so the block's loop read the same token again, forever. Since `0ba7b084`
# a failed statement drops what is left of its line.
# The shape: `elif` over a body, after an `if`. The `unexpected_block` below
# the `elif` is the parser's not reading `elif` as `else if`, which is
# grammar_expr's and given to lane 132 the same day; the swap itself is
# certain here, an `if` above it and a condition of its own.
# Corrected 2026-09-29 at the coordinator's gate of lane 132 merged with the
# trunk: lane 132 reads `elif` as `else if` where the swap is certain, so
# the block below it is its body and the `unexpected_block` above is gone;
# one mistake, one message.

function main()
    if 1 == 1
        print(1)
    elif 2 == 2  #~ reserved_word
        print(2)
